ce profiles of SR-SPR at various replay ratios, demonstrating that replay ratio scaling consistently improves performance up to at least replay ratio 16. We also compare a version of SR-SPR that uses replay ratio 16 to standard baselines and recent work (Micheli et al., 2022) in table 2. SR-SPR establishes a new state-of-the-art for model-free control on Atari 100k, and rivals prior work that has aggressively pretrained on additional data (Liu & Abbeel, 2021; Schwarzer et al., 2021b). We present full results and per-game scores for SR-SPR in table 4, and show aggregated training curves in fig. 16."
